  "worked_solution": "The matrix $B$ is singular if and only if $det(B)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B) & =1\\cdot (2x-4)-2\\cdot (3x+2) \\\\  & =2x-4-6x-4 \\\\  & =-4x-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4x-8 & =0 \\\\ -4x & =8 \\\\ x & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
